@ ---- LBL :TABLE: key 6 after a verdict (R96 = 1): the truth table of the variables used, in the small font: the
@ formula on top, then 2^n rows (up to 64: four columns of 16), each "1 0 1 | 1" (the variables in the order
@ p..u, the first one changing slowest, all true first; then the formula's value Φ), a header over each column,
@ BLOCK 1-4 under the columns (when there are more than one).
@ Row k (2^n - 1 down to 0): the j-th variable used takes bit n - 1 - j of k; the bit of the word R24 to read is
@ m = the sum of 2^code over the variables true in the row (code 0-5: p-u, bit i of row m is variable i).
@ Any key goes back: the formula, the soft keys and the verdict drawn again. LBL / DSE / GTO loops (10 DO already).
@ R47 ">" then the code letters of the variables used, R34 the header, R40 n, R41 the rows left (2^n down to 1),
@ R38 k, R43 j (n down to 1), R45 m, R48 the row's place (0 up), R33 the row's text, R49 a bit, R42 work ----
